@k.alpha-contract:K{ap=[transparent_sprites_75353d50,glows_19e4066b,sprite_atlases_07b42f1f];ck=[~75:Binary-alpha assets contain only 0 and 255 unless an exception is declared.,~56:Composited fixtures agree with the declared alpha model.];nm=~38:Declare alpha and compositing behavior;op=[~55:Keep alpha policy separate from RGB palette membership.,~84:Use the chosen compositing equation consistently through export, import and display.,~73:Inspect edges against light and dark backgrounds after round-trip import.];rk=[~78:Fully transparent RGB channels can differ without changing visible appearance.,~59:Multiplying premultiplied RGB by alpha again darkens edges.];rq=[~78:RGBA interpretation, straight or premultiplied alpha, and allowed alpha levels];so=[@s9607720391d7364f4ce0,@s3ebf4844fd3d465b52ec,@scabcd5fb54fa40c4ce6d,@s4cf9d4a55c2ba014c0ec];tg=[~14:alpha-contract]}
@k.animation-anchors:K{ap=[walk_cycles_e3b8ebff,idle_loops_012679ae,weapon_actions_62ab60be];ck=[~70:Required planted contacts remain fixed through their contact interval.,~71:The loop boundary obeys the same motion policy as internal transitions.];nm=~38:Track contacts and review loop closure;op=[~79:Track contact-point coordinates independently from each frame's crop rectangle.,~90:Use onion-skin or difference views to compare adjacent poses and last-to-first transition.,~78:Permit displacement where the action demands it; lock only specified contacts.];pc=[@e.animation-anchors];rk=[~91:A moving root can coexist with a visually planted foot only after world-space compensation.,~67:A low pixel-difference score does not prove a convincing animation.];rq=[~57:Named anchors, ground line and expected contact intervals];so=[@s9607720391d7364f4ce0,@s48f5dcc4ea69b34d361b,@s1c92686e53e5646d9ee3];tg=[~17:animation-anchors]}
@k.asset-provenance:K{ap=[reference_derived_assets_3b7d9e7b,legacy_snippets_5a32b20c,variant_libraries_90013dce];ck=[~72:Every reused external component has its source and reuse basis recorded.,~66:Adaptations identify which parts were reused, redrawn or excluded.];nm=~55:Carry source and adaptation intent into reusable assets;op=[~78:Preserve the original material and record the exact excerpt used as reference.,~77:Separate original creative examples from third-party imagery, fonts and code.,~137:Record reuse permission evidence when distributing sourced material; if it is absent, author an original asset from the functional brief.];rk=[~66:An inspiration URL or a copied snippet is not a license statement.,~85:Legacy Waylight colors and UI mandates are project-specific, not universal art rules.];rq=[~88:Original source path, creator information if supplied, intended use and adaptation scope];so=[@s9607720391d7364f4ce0,@scbfe277b31644a34a152,@s97f77d3ca37ac92a5bcf,@se2ad479cf7f5b0467a1e,@s97e3489cef499820d0c5];tg=[~16:asset-provenance]}
@k.atlas-reuse-budget:K{ap=[large_modular_actors_75f8c128,sprite_libraries_dab972f8,reused_animation_states_0b96ced6];ck=[~45:Source rectangles reconstruct original parts.,~95:Performance claims include measured conditions and the relevant format or compression settings.];nm=~53:Atlas compatible parts and measure actual render cost;op=[~59:Deduplicate identical raster states using content identity.,~78:Pack compatible parts with deliberate padding and matching companion channels.,~91:Measure memory, draw calls, texture switches and transform costs on the target integration.];rk=[~109:An atlas does not guarantee one draw call; blending, ordering, shaders and renderer limits can split batches.,~77:Uncompressed byte arithmetic is an estimate, not resident memory measurement.];rq=[~75:Texture formats, atlas bounds, material groups and measured target renderer];so=[@s9607720391d7364f4ce0,@sf06d7882335c7a5e3e88,@scabcd5fb54fa40c4ce6d];tg=[~18:atlas-reuse-budget]}
@k.cell-materials:K{ap=[falling_sand_aa7d9365,destructible_materials_8be0910c,cellular_worlds_1b5de0a4];ck=[~49:Every nonempty cell resolves to a known material.,~69:Palette changes cannot change physics merely by changing visible RGB.];nm=~59:Use shared material definitions with per-cell mutable state;op=[~66:Put immutable density or phase thresholds in material definitions.,~90:Store occupancy, temperature, lifetime and ownership only where the simulation needs them.,~98:Derive appearance from material and state without conflating render colors with material identity.];pc=[@e.cell-materials];rk=[~88:The shared-table layout is a proposed architecture, not a confirmed Noita memory layout.,~46:Decorative dust may need only a visual effect.];rq=[~55:Material IDs, behavior table and declared mutable state];so=[@s9607720391d7364f4ce0,@s5fbad44ce7f75d25cb0f,@s6a57d2b1eb08a6832662];tg=[~14:cell-materials]}
@k.cluster-handoff:K{ap=[tiny_highlights_75f843c3,eyes_d8fe183f,one_pixel_feature_motion_e0c41a77];ck=[~54:The feature remains connected under the declared rule.,~90:Its centroid moves toward the target and any area change stays inside the declared budget.];nm=~49:Move a feature using a deliberate cluster handoff;op=[~68:Establish the leading pixels before withdrawing the trailing pixels.,~82:For narrow features use approved shade transitions if area growth is unacceptable.,~52:Protect surrounding silhouette and feature identity.];pc=[@e.cluster-handoff];rk=[~70:Temporary widening changes volume and may be wrong for rigid material.,~62:A mechanically valid handoff still needs visual timing review.];rq=[~67:Feature mask, permitted temporary area change and connectivity rule];so=[@s9607720391d7364f4ce0,@s5f5100009a28ecbdb89e,@s93a557df2c855f76aaf1];tg=[~15:cluster-handoff]}
@k.companion-alignment:K{ap=[diffuse_normal_pairs_4bc6fdc1,height_maps_ccec93e4,mask_atlases_a3a4d09f,animated_lighting_b38861e4];ck=[~97:Dimensions, original sizes, trim offsets, pivots and frame IDs agree where shared UVs require it.,~72:A channel sampled at a diffuse feature corresponds to that same feature.];nm=~39:Keep all sampled asset channels aligned;op=[~74:Apply the same crop, packing and frame ordering to corresponding channels.,~47:Represent missing optional channels explicitly.,~79:Use recognizable calibration marks to check sample correspondence after import.];rk=[~46:Equal dimensions alone do not prove alignment.,~103:Independently packed textures can be valid only when the renderer has an explicit mapping between them.];rq=[~67:Shared canvas, frame IDs, trim offsets, pivots and atlas rectangles];so=[@s9607720391d7364f4ce0,@scabcd5fb54fa40c4ce6d,@sd1694b303e428f8964ae];tg=[~19:companion-alignment]}
@k.composed-animation:K{ap=[boss_animation_8b678ba8,weapon_actions_during_locomotion_47e9c9d8,damage_variants_a3339652];ck=[~60:Every animated property has an unambiguous composition rule.,~52:Changing one channel does not reset unrelated state.];nm=~58:Compose independent motion channels with defined ownership;op=[~78:Assign locomotion, aim, recoil, damage and secondary motion to named channels.,~76:Define override or additive behavior when channels affect the same property.,~93:Keep attachment swaps independent of unrelated loop phase unless the action requires a reset.];rk=[~71:Independent clips still require coordination for contacts and overlaps.,~85:Conflicting channel writes create order-dependent results unless resolved explicitly.];rq=[~56:Channel priorities, affected properties and event inputs];so=[@s9607720391d7364f4ce0,@s72271c1f146375825a21];tg=[~18:composed-animation]}
@k.continuous-state-final-snap:K{ap=[pixel_rigs_a03d93a4,camera_motion_b83bcf1a,procedural_recoil_2ef0ed6a];ck=[~59:Rendering does not overwrite simulation or animation state.,~71:Final positions align to the declared grid with bounded rounding error.];nm=~55:Keep continuous motion and quantize its final placement;op=[~54:Evaluate continuous parent and child transforms first.,~82:Apply camera transformation before the declared screen-grid quantization boundary.,~46:Retain unsnapped state for subsequent updates.];pc=[@e.continuous-state-final-snap];rk=[~49:Snapping every bone independently can open seams.,~77:Tie rounding differs across languages; specify it for deterministic fixtures.];rq=[~77:Floating-point state, logical scale, camera transform and rounding tie policy];so=[@s9607720391d7364f4ce0,@sccb41de8b50ef76c241a,@s697bc67218e996283b3e];tg=[~27:continuous-state-final-snap]}
@k.coverage-candidates:K{ap=[subpixel_translation_a94e1ea2,candidate_in_betweens_1c4ef46b];ck=[~45:Zero shift reconstructs the source occupancy.,~95:Translation preserves total coverage before clipping and output dimensions remain logical size.];nm=~55:Generate constrained supersampled in-between candidates;op=[~48:Replicate occupancy to a 4x or 8x coverage grid.,~108:Apply integer shifts in that grid, average coverage back to logical cells, and quantize to an approved ramp.,~74:Run feature, palette and silhouette checks before any artistic acceptance.];pc=[@e.coverage-candidates];rk=[~75:Supersampling produces candidates; it is not proof of a hand-authored look.,~89:Clipping at canvas bounds must be explicit; ramp quantization can change apparent volume.];rq=[~81:Integer scale factor, source occupancy, approved coverage ramp and cleanup policy];so=[@s9607720391d7364f4ce0,@sd974a5639d2ee1c693c0];tg=[~19:coverage-candidates]}
@k.crop-and-anchor:K{ap=[background_removal_6fcdd33a,sprite_extraction_61fea8aa,trimmed_animation_frames_cdbcb207];ck=[~55:Restored pixels and anchors match the untrimmed source.,~84:No intentionally translucent edge is discarded without an explicit threshold policy.];nm=~57:Trim transparent padding while preserving logical anchors;op=[~74:Find the permitted opaque bounds and record trim offset and original size.,~58:Translate pivot and socket coordinates by the crop origin.,~84:Keep restoration metadata so each frame can be reconstructed on its original canvas.];pc=[@e.crop-and-anchor];rk=[~73:A tighter image rectangle can move the sprite if its trim offset is lost.,~106:Removing a background requires an actual mask decision, not blindly treating one RGB color as transparent.];rq=[~75:Original canvas, alpha policy and an anchor in original logical coordinates];so=[@s9607720391d7364f4ce0,@se2ad479cf7f5b0467a1e,@s48f5dcc4ea69b34d361b,@scabcd5fb54fa40c4ce6d];tg=[~15:crop-and-anchor]}
@k.destruction-topology:K{ap=[destructible_structures_7edc2652,cell_to_body_conversion_abcf4b6d];ck=[~66:Component union equals the remaining occupancy with no duplicates.,~69:Every occupied cell has exactly one owner at the conversion boundary.];nm=~62:Extract components and preserve occupancy at solver boundaries;op=[~52:Identify connected occupied components after damage.,~109:Extract boundaries with an explicit treatment of diagonal ambiguity, then simplify within gameplay tolerance.,~66:Transfer ownership once and retain a mapping back to source cells.];pc=[@e.destruction-topology];rk=[~69:Component extraction alone does not prove stable rigid-body behavior.,~101:Contour simplification and rerasterization can alter collision shape; measure their error explicitly.];rq=[~88:Connectivity convention, ownership transfer, contour policy and simplification tolerance];so=[@s9607720391d7364f4ce0,@s99fd2be46c4b18acf3b5,@s1bb55e846680d8654057];tg=[~20:destruction-topology]}
@k.deterministic-cell-update:K{ap=[falling_sand_aa7d9365,liquid_rules_90bc72e8,replayable_cellular_simulation_cba919a0];ck=[~66:Material count is conserved for nonreactive closed-world movement.,~99:No material entity exceeds its per-tick displacement bound; repeated runs with the same seed match.];nm=~44:Bound movement and prevent duplicate updates;op=[~47:Process gravity rules in a declared scan order.,~95:Carry update identity with moving material so it cannot move twice unintentionally in one tick.,~72:Resolve target conflicts deterministically and record boundary behavior.];pc=[@e.deterministic-cell-update];rk=[~70:Bottom-up order alone does not prevent all cross-chunk double updates.,~80:Deterministic ties do not make different algorithms or update orders equivalent.];rq=[~78:Tick identifiers, movement bounds, seeded tie-breaking and conflict resolution];so=[@s9607720391d7364f4ce0,@s2e8f8fc26f8aa41ce39d,@s42bdea7656b569140bed];tg=[~25:deterministic-cell-update]}
@k.dirty-region-wakeup:K{ap=[large_mostly_static_cellular_worlds_f9c5ba14];ck=[~77:Optimized and full-scan outputs agree for the same declared update semantics.,~58:Boundary activity wakes every region that can be affected.];nm=~48:Track active regions using rule influence bounds;op=[~66:Dirty both source and destination neighborhoods when cells change.,~67:Expand the dirty region by the complete next-step influence radius.,~70:Sleep stable regions and wake neighboring chunks for boundary changes.];rk=[~69:64x64 is a source case-study choice, not a universal best chunk size.,~103:Counting fewer cell visits demonstrates less scanning, not automatically faster wall-clock performance.];rq=[~94:Chunk size, complete read/write radius, cross-boundary wake rules and reference full-scan mode];so=[@s9607720391d7364f4ce0,@s31ea9e0e495b246b0c57];tg=[~19:dirty-region-wakeup]}
@k.dither-coverage:K{ap=[limited_palette_gradients_bd5b950c,intentional_texture_255b0db4,ordered_translucency_cca3fe72];ck=[~66:Coverage is the actual selected-cell count divided by total cells.,~50:The pattern changes only within its semantic mask.];nm=~46:Count dither coverage and constrain its region;op=[~72:Use the 4x4 rank matrix [[0,8,2,10],[12,4,14,6],[3,11,1,9],[15,7,13,5]].,~68:For fraction q, select cells with rank < 16*q when 16*q is integral.,~96:Keep the pattern phase consistent across adjacent regions unless a discontinuity is intentional.];pc=[@e.dither-coverage];rk=[~80:The local source's example percentage labels are incorrect; count cells instead.,~77:Dither can add noise and is optional; flat clusters may suit an asset better.];rq=[~66:A tileable threshold matrix, two approved colors and a region mask];so=[@s9607720391d7364f4ce0,@s43d4515c06262eb87579,@s9516d3a19e94a5313eab];tg=[~15:dither-coverage]}
@k.dither-phase-motion:K{ap=[water_texture_163b558d,energy_fields_9eb7cb3d,controlled_translucency_b3f63777];ck=[~47:Every phase preserves the specified population.,~54:After one period the original pattern returns exactly.];nm=~44:Animate dither phase with an explicit period;op=[~67:Shift the pattern phase deterministically with wrapped coordinates.,~49:Hold coverage constant when changing phase alone.,~84:Keep stable regions untouched and preview the result at its intended scale and rate.];pc=[@e.dither-phase-motion];rk=[~46:Unseeded per-frame noise causes temporal boil.,~102:Constant coverage and perfect looping do not prove that flicker is comfortable or artistically useful.];rq=[~70:A fixed threshold matrix, motion direction, region and positive period];so=[@s9607720391d7364f4ce0,@s43d4515c06262eb87579,@sfb2426549ca6c3a6fd62];tg=[~19:dither-phase-motion]}
@k.edge-color-migration:K{ap=[slow_movement_73712330,small_contours_0ad9a50f,subpixel_animation_candidates_21643862];ck=[~59:Intermediate frames stay in the palette and feature region.,~57:The chosen motion metric moves in the intended direction.];nm=~50:Encode fractional edge motion with approved colors;op=[~87:Construct coverage changes for the selected edge while keeping output on integer cells.,~38:Map coverage to approved ramp entries.,~96:Measure a luminance- or coverage-weighted centroid and inspect the motion at authored durations.];pc=[@e.edge-color-migration];rk=[~59:Apparent motion depends on contrast and viewing conditions.,~80:This method does not place a physical sprite at a fractional logical coordinate.];rq=[~52:Known background, edge ramp and an edge feature mask];so=[@s9607720391d7364f4ce0,@s796e540bb76171f05a7f,@sf1496a8bcdeb568f888f];tg=[~20:edge-color-migration]}
@k.edge-rhythm:K{ap=[clean_linework_08dea3fe,small_curved_forms_e37a2e1c,hard_silhouettes_99485584];ck=[~73:A supplied straight diagonal retains its declared repeating step pattern.,~43:No protected corner changes during cleanup.];nm=~56:Audit stair-step runs without imposing one contour style;op=[~60:Trace boundary runs and highlight sudden run-length changes.,~52:Regularize only contours intended to read as smooth.,~71:Preserve corners, damage and organic asymmetry identified in the brief.];rk=[~68:Not every uneven run is a jaggy; shape can require an abrupt change.,~58:Mechanical contour smoothing can erase style and identity.];rq=[~68:A contour mask and declared intentional corners or irregular regions];so=[@s9607720391d7364f4ce0,@s0c9cbf55db7ffca6a99b,@s61700d0924ea235e5b2c];tg=[~11:edge-rhythm]}
@k.frame-timing:K{ap=[sprite_animation_9537e27d,attacks_ced7c095,idle_loops_012679ae,ui_feedback_adf3d2c9];ck=[~85:Every duration is positive and playback reaches the expected frame at boundary times.,~64:One-shot terminal states and looping wrap behavior are explicit.];nm=~45:Author duration and event semantics per frame;op=[~60:Store durations explicitly rather than assuming uniform FPS.,~67:Name anticipation, action, impact and settle events where relevant.,~80:Define half-open time intervals so event and frame boundaries have no ambiguity.];pc=[@e.frame-timing];rk=[~63:More frames do not automatically improve weight or readability.,~62:Unspecified preview FPS must not overwrite authored durations.];rq=[~65:Ordered frame IDs, positive durations and loop or one-shot policy];so=[@s9607720391d7364f4ce0,@sc1d1c26ee857f5299b97,@s0334631fec4ca6cf3e35];tg=[~12:frame-timing]}
@k.integer-presentation:K{ap=[strict_grid_games_a7cd2a47,pixel_previews_014b1177,sprite_delivery_638f99a7];ck=[~75:A logical pixel expands into a uniform scale-by-scale block in the fixture.,~64:No new colors appear during opaque nearest-neighbor enlargement.];nm=~59:Render at a declared logical grid and inspect device pixels;op=[~87:Render or sample at the logical grid, then use a declared integer scale where required.,~83:Apply nearest sampling to image scaling and account for browser device pixel ratio.,~68:Inspect the final output, not only a CSS property or import setting.];pc=[@e.integer-presentation];rk=[~63:Nearest filtering alone does not constrain lighting resolution.,~90:Noninteger scaling, arbitrary rotation and browser zoom can change displayed pixel widths.];rq=[~68:Logical resolution, camera convention and target viewport dimensions];so=[@s9607720391d7364f4ce0,@s78b769959c29731360b2,@s6392e4accd471f225f3a,@s697bc67218e996283b3e];tg=[~20:integer-presentation]}
@k.material-channel-budget:K{ap=[a_2_5d_assets_abb1ddf4,lamps_dfe0b81f,lava_5ed45566,material_effects_cb439ae4];ck=[~68:Every declared channel has a named consumer and documented fallback.,~79:Response-mask zero suppresses the masked term; emission follows its own policy.];nm=~58:Add height, masks and emission only with defined consumers;op=[~67:Keep color, direction, height, response mask and emission distinct.,~65:Declare packing and whether values are color data or linear data.,~97:Reject unsupported channels at integration rather than silently treating them as active features.];pc=[@e.material-channel-budget];rk=[~67:Extra channels increase authoring, memory and synchronization work.,~91:An image generator returning a map does not establish that an engine consumes it correctly.];rq=[~79:Per-channel meaning, numeric range, coordinate convention and renderer consumer];so=[@s9607720391d7364f4ce0,@s3ebf4844fd3d465b52ec,@se82d234af07d683238a3,@s223bae26a90f3f56d122];tg=[~23:material-channel-budget]}
@k.material-ramps:K{ap=[recoloring_7ad2d6ee,shaded_sprites_331bace0,palette_lighting_28f9e4d9];ck=[~47:Ramp lookup never escapes its assigned palette.,~64:A recolor preserves the declared ordering and region membership.];nm=~41:Use material-specific value and hue ramps;op=[~63:Build dark-to-light ramps appropriate to the material and mood.,~70:Assign each material's pixels to its ramp and retain semantic indices.,~99:Use hue shifts only where the art direction calls for them; inspect neighboring materials together.];pc=[@e.material-ramps];rk=[~102:Hue shifting and monotonically increasing numerical luminance are choices, not universal requirements.,~70:Different materials may intentionally share colors or intersect ramps.];rq=[~55:Named material regions and approved ordered color ramps];so=[@s9607720391d7364f4ce0,@s621d534400fd84e4a15e,@sb7365f656b25902176ab];tg=[~14:material-ramps]}
@k.normal-direction:K{ap=[normal_mapped_sprites_7bf74c92,a_2_5d_surfaces_67ade9c2];ck=[~60:Decoded vectors are finite and unit length within tolerance.,~79:A right-facing slope responds more strongly to right-side than left-side light.];nm=~51:Validate normal encoding and coordinate orientation;op=[~70:Treat normal channels as direction data under the importer convention.,~68:Decode and normalize with a defined fallback for degenerate vectors.,~79:Use a directional fixture to validate handedness and green-channel orientation.];pc=[@e.normal-direction];rk=[~66:Applying an sRGB transfer curve to normal data changes directions.,~79:An 8-bit flat normal is approximate; compare with quantization-aware tolerance.];rq=[~74:Normal axis convention, color-space interpretation and unit-vector decoder];so=[@s9607720391d7364f4ce0,@s92b3ab94a73587889026,@s9141a03fbece511cb804];tg=[~16:normal-direction]}
@k.palette-contract:K{ap=[indexed_sprites_40eaa310,limited_palette_styles_c8701d42,material_ramps_1ca01010];ck=[~45:Every checked pixel maps to an allowed index.,~64:Palette changes retain stable semantic meaning and transparency.];nm=~37:Declare and validate a scoped palette;op=[~75:Assign stable palette indices and reserve any transparent entry explicitly.,~96:Validate opaque pixels against the palette; keep lighting-output exemptions separately declared.,~85:Apply color replacements by semantic ramp rather than unrestricted RGB interpolation.];pc=[@e.palette-contract];rk=[~89:A fixed small palette is optional art direction, not a universal definition of pixel art.,~74:RGBA data can be palette-constrained without using an indexed file format.];rq=[~68:An approved RGBA palette, color-space choice and transparency policy];so=[@s9607720391d7364f4ce0,@s621d534400fd84e4a15e,@s1f5d930626daa8ca27aa,@s44583b3f97acfcced242];tg=[~16:palette-contract]}
@k.palette-lighting:K{ap=[stylized_dynamic_lighting_03e113af,strict_output_palettes_2c42d882];ck=[~47:Band index remains in 0..K-1 for finite inputs.,~44:Ramp-output mode emits only declared colors.];nm=~59:Quantize light response and optionally select palette ramps;op=[~74:Compute or accept continuous light intensity separately from raster color.,~58:Clamp intensity to the declared range before quantization.,~126:For strict palette output choose a material ramp entry; multiplying RGB by a band does not itself preserve palette membership.];pc=[@e.palette-lighting];rk=[~67:Banding can shimmer as a light moves; inspect temporal transitions.,~52:Lighting quantization is an optional style decision.];rq=[~73:Finite intensity, K>=2 bands, clamping policy and optional material ramps];so=[@s9607720391d7364f4ce0,@s0fd84e2d189b06f2248f];tg=[~16:palette-lighting]}
@k.phased-write-ownership:K{ap=[parallel_cellular_simulation_a5cf2c2e];ck=[~58:Every concurrent pair has empty write-domain intersection.,~122:A serial execution of the same phase ordering agrees with its parallel implementation when deterministic mode is promised.];nm=~61:Schedule only disjoint writable cellular regions concurrently;op=[~84:Compute each job's possible write domain, including halos and cascaded rule effects.,~48:Group jobs only when these domains are disjoint.,~91:Place required barriers between phases and re-evaluate ownership if movement bounds change.];pc=[@e.phased-write-ownership];rk=[~70:Copying four phases is unsafe when a different rule can write farther.,~90:Rectangular halo estimates may be conservative; smaller shapes need proof, not assumption.];rq=[~67:Exact job write domains, maximum displacement and barrier semantics];so=[@s9607720391d7364f4ce0,@sbc523b27ef4cf532d972];tg=[~22:phased-write-ownership]}
@k.pipeline-order:K{ap=[combined_pixel_systems_302f11bb,engine_integration_aa7bd944];ck=[~72:No stage reads data before its producer or ownership transfer completes.,~123:Continuous animation precedes final snapping; quantized lighting precedes final enlargement when that pipeline is selected.];nm=~68:Validate dependency order across simulation, animation and rendering;op=[~131:Name simulation updates, structural conversion, animation evaluation, snapping, lighting and final presentation as separate stages.,~90:Schedule according to actual dependencies and document any engine-specific feedback cycle.,~81:Validate declared stage order and require capabilities for each requested output.];rk=[~80:The source sequence is a proposal; engine physics order may legitimately differ.,~58:A metadata declaration is not evidence that any stage ran.];rq=[~52:Stage dependency graph and ownership transfer points];so=[@s9607720391d7364f4ce0,@s191d295239d4054cbb8c,@se7acfd0f2dd6a7979a0d];tg=[~14:pipeline-order]}
@k.preserve-authored-shading:K{ap=[hand_shaded_sprites_4c98f64c,hybrid_pixel_lighting_c5cd36d0];ck=[~41:Zero modulation reproduces diffuse input.,~70:Any palette or value clamps are explicit and applied after modulation.];nm=~53:Declare how dynamic light combines with baked shading;op=[~58:Record whether volume already exists in the diffuse image.,~57:Choose dynamic-light modulation appropriate to that mode.,~83:Compare baseline, neutral-light and opposing-light states to detect double shading.];pc=[@e.preserve-authored-shading];rk=[~65:A generated normal map can interpret painted shadows as geometry.,~82:Strong dynamic lighting can contradict highlights already painted into the sprite.];rq=[~76:Authored-shade, flat-albedo or hybrid mode and a bounded modulation strength];so=[@s9607720391d7364f4ce0,@s6c5b18c505a00398fabe,@s3ebf4844fd3d465b52ec];tg=[~25:preserve-authored-shading]}
@k.reaction-tables:K{ap=[thermal_worlds_f25125a8,material_chemistry_e8c9b182,emergent_effects_0e1fd681];ck=[~60:Unknown materials and invalid probabilities fail validation.,~59:Reaction outcomes occur only when declared conditions hold.];nm=~41:Encode material reactions as bounded data;op=[~61:Separate immutable reaction definitions from live cell state.,~91:Validate references, probability ranges, temperature conditions and available output space.,~73:Define reaction priority and accounting rules before combining reactions.];rk=[~97:Gameplay chemistry need not conserve real chemical mass, but its own accounting must be explicit.,~68:Different reaction order can change results even with the same seed.];rq=[~87:Known reactants, conditions, output materials, probability policy and conflict ordering];so=[@s9607720391d7364f4ce0,@s534eda8ec0493cc5a402,@s6a57d2b1eb08a6832662];tg=[~15:reaction-tables]}
@k.representation-owner:K{ap=[all_asset_briefs_60e49b74];ck=[~76:Every requested behavior has an owner and an explicit input/output contract.,~90:A decorative effect does not acquire physical simulation merely because it looks granular.];nm=~49:Choose the representation that owns each behavior;op=[~154:Classify independently moving matter as cells, shape-preserving parts as attachments, pose-dependent topology as frames, and surface response as channels.,~85:Record multiple owners when one asset spans systems and name the conversion boundary.];rk=[~101:This classification recommends an architecture; it does not make PixelLab or a renderer implement it.,~51:A single asset may require several representations.];rq=[~64:A brief naming visual, physical, animation and lighting behavior];so=[@s9607720391d7364f4ce0,@s79c5c710d285828d9512,@se621a49aafbf8356c10e,@se7acfd0f2dd6a7979a0d];tg=[~20:representation-owner]}
@k.rig-cutout:K{ap=[large_machines_aee44191,segmented_creatures_b1896de3,equipment_variants_6c7a3e2c];ck=[~54:Every transformed part has a defined parent and pivot.,~93:Topology-changing poses select explicit artwork rather than relying on accidental resampling.];nm=~55:Separate rigid parts from topology-changing attachments;op=[~61:Identify regions whose pixels remain unchanged during motion.,~94:Represent those as rigid attachments; redraw joints, faces or openings whose topology changes.,~62:Keep bone hierarchy and visible attachment selection distinct.];pc=[@e.rig-cutout];rk=[~112:Weighted mesh deformation may be valid for a chosen style but does not preserve authored clusters automatically.,~54:The local Metal Slug-specific rig claim is unverified.];rq=[~75:A part hierarchy, visible attachment states and intended deformation policy];so=[@s9607720391d7364f4ce0,@s07add3bb20e7a42aed52,@s64493f7684f8396d09c3];tg=[~10:rig-cutout]}
@k.rig-sockets:K{ap=[interchangeable_limbs_f0ef7c84,weapons_167a79b5,modular_bosses_2efd9031];ck=[~83:Every valid swap preserves the socket world position within the declared tolerance.,~58:Unknown sockets or incompatible part tags fail explicitly.];nm=~53:Define pivot and socket coordinates in logical pixels;op=[~73:Store socket and pivot values in the same explicit coordinate convention.,~83:Position the child so its transformed pivot equals the parent's transformed socket.,~55:Recalculate attachment pivots when trim offsets change.];pc=[@e.rig-sockets];rk=[~121:Integer-valued pivots are not universally correct; even-size centers may be half-integer under a pixel-center convention.,~59:Mirroring may require semantic left/right socket remapping.];rq=[~91:Coordinate origin, pixel-center or pixel-corner convention, parent sockets and child pivots];so=[@s9607720391d7364f4ce0,@s48f5dcc4ea69b34d361b,@s09502f4d1dc3dc7df77a];tg=[~11:rig-sockets]}
@k.rotation-policy:K{ap=[aiming_weapons_9f6c4633,rotating_machinery_23088087,directional_actors_ab994558];ck=[~47:All rendered angles follow the chosen strategy.,~81:Every required orientation is covered, and pixel crawl is reviewed where allowed.];nm=~40:Choose a rotation strategy for each part;op=[~109:Choose continuous nearest sampling, quantized angles, hand-drawn directions or an intermediate render target.,~45:Document which visual changes are acceptable.,~64:Evaluate extreme and intermediate poses around the actual pivot.];pc=[@e.rotation-policy];rk=[~77:Nearest sampling and a snapped pivot do not make arbitrary rotation lossless.,~85:A 90-degree rotation can preserve texels while changing directional lighting meaning.];rq=[~62:Permitted angles, silhouette tolerance and target logical grid];so=[@s9607720391d7364f4ce0,@s3f11d7dbcd1bbdd3a091,@s3aa0b999b7b18870a825];tg=[~15:rotation-policy]}
@k.selective-edge-aa:K{ap=[subpixel_edges_cb6d504d,curves_against_known_backgrounds_6fcf945e];ck=[~62:Changed pixels stay within the selected edge mask and palette.,~43:Protected hard edges remain byte-identical.];nm=~55:Apply authored edge antialiasing only to selected edges;op=[~86:Choose intermediate colors from the approved ramp inside the selected boundary region.,~80:Preserve required hard edges and avoid universal outlines of intermediate color.,~57:Preview against each allowed background before accepting.];rk=[~80:Background-specific intermediate colors can form halos on different backgrounds.,~88:This is authored color placement, not a permission to enable bilinear texture filtering.];rq=[~59:Approved edge ramp, edge mask and representative background];so=[@s9607720391d7364f4ce0,@s796e540bb76171f05a7f,@s78b769959c29731360b2];tg=[~17:selective-edge-aa]}
@k.semantic-clusters:K{ap=[sprite_cleanup_d4949c19,protected_eyes_3d8487f0,material_boundaries_234882e3,micro_animation_7168ed12];ck=[~44:Connected-component counts are reproducible.,~56:Protected feature masks remain present after operations.];nm=~58:Track raster connectivity and semantic clusters separately;op=[~63:Extract same-color connected components with the selected rule.,~88:Label intentional details such as eyes, sparks and stars; these may be legal singletons.,~82:Use semantic masks across multiple colors when a feature must be edited as a unit.];pc=[@e.semantic-clusters];rk=[~66:A semantic cluster need not be a single-color connected component.,~66:Automatically deleting every singleton destroys legitimate detail.];rq=[~51:A declared 4- or 8-neighbor rule and semantic masks];so=[@s9607720391d7364f4ce0,@s522ab9a3a0370edee9f5,@s61700d0924ea235e5b2c];tg=[~17:semantic-clusters]}
@k.shading-drift:K{ap=[breathing_idles_9072d861,slow_turns_3e231f6f,cloth_or_muscle_motion_9df2c401];ck=[~58:Protected silhouette and identity pixels remain unchanged.,~57:All changed pixels belong to the declared shading region.];nm=~52:Animate internal shading while protecting silhouette;op=[~77:Keep the outer occupancy stable for a subtle idle when the brief requires it.,~51:Shift only selected internal highlights or shadows.,~94:Review whether shading motion communicates form or incorrectly looks like moving illumination.];pc=[@e.shading-drift];rk=[~68:Highlight movement may imply changing light rather than body motion.,~81:Silhouette preservation is a local idle constraint, not a general animation rule.];rq=[~65:Opaque mask, semantic highlight or shadow mask and approved ramps];so=[@s9607720391d7364f4ce0,@sfe52e56959af3855bdbc,@sa3f987a9675a4299019a];tg=[~13:shading-drift]}
@k.shadow-visibility:K{ap=[shadow_casting_props_6e4cf652,walls_5fbffcac,dynamic_lights_58368a72];ck=[~61:A normal-only asset cannot satisfy a shadow-casting contract.,~89:Removing the occluder changes visibility while leaving surface normal response unchanged.];nm=~40:Separate surface response from occlusion;op=[~54:Evaluate orientation and visibility as separate terms.,~83:Require an actual visibility representation when the asset declares shadow casting.,~81:Choose caster simplification and light-resolution policy appropriate to the game.];pc=[@e.shadow-visibility];rk=[~62:A dark diffuse patch is not evidence of a dynamic cast shadow.,~62:Normal maps do not encode which other object blocks the light.];rq=[~85:An explicit caster polygon, occupancy field, depth or other visibility representation];so=[@s9607720391d7364f4ce0,@s4d9d9baff7b1b459e6a1,@s199c3e97537aa4cc6720];tg=[~17:shadow-visibility]}
@k.sheet-metadata:K{ap=[spritesheets_16aafbd4,tilesets_85cbc0d7,atlas_import_95f7d6a2];ck=[~49:Each referenced frame is present and addressable.,~60:Round-trip extraction preserves expected pixels and anchors.];nm=~45:Make sheet layout and frame identity explicit;op=[~53:Store frame rectangles and stable IDs with the sheet.,~80:Validate in-bounds rectangles, intended overlaps, frame order and trim metadata.,~85:Extract frames and reconstruct the logical originals before using a sheet in runtime.];pc=[@e.sheet-metadata];rk=[~73:A PNG sheet alone does not communicate playback duration, pivots or tags.,~60:Packed atlas order can differ from semantic animation order.];rq=[~72:Image dimensions, frame rectangles, offset, spacing, margin and ordering];so=[@s9607720391d7364f4ce0,@scabcd5fb54fa40c4ce6d,@s05456bb516e3f7f3549f];tg=[~14:sheet-metadata]}
@k.silhouette-readability:K{ap=[characters_25d939ff,inventory_icons_f7812ea4,interactive_props_25a44283];ck=[~59:Named identity landmarks remain visible at the target size.,~79:Required gaps stay open and interactive forms separate from their surroundings.];nm=~57:Evaluate identity using silhouette and target backgrounds;op=[~43:Render a flat opaque mask before detailing.,~91:Inspect major proportions, negative spaces and landmark separation at native logical scale.,~77:Compare the colored asset on representative light, dark and busy backgrounds.];rk=[~66:Silhouette alone cannot validate faces, materials or fine symbols.,~62:No contrast ratio or component count proves aesthetic quality.];rq=[~73:Intended viewing scale, representative backgrounds and identity landmarks];so=[@s9607720391d7364f4ce0,@s61700d0924ea235e5b2c,@sa3f987a9675a4299019a,@s874004913199562fa7a0];tg=[~22:silhouette-readability]}
@k.state-driven-pixel-ui:K{ap=[pixel_interaction_prompts_020831fc,health_icons_2ef86a03,selected_project_ui_80730ea8];ck=[~67:The visual state corresponds to the supplied input or health state.,~71:No decorative timer reports an event or progress that has not occurred.];nm=~48:Tie pixel UI animation to actual state and input;op=[~72:Map idle, pressed, disabled and health states to explicit visual states.,~60:Use timing only for the transition the real event triggered.,~82:Retain static recognizability and adapt scale and color across the surrounding UI.];rk=[~88:The archive's keyboard prompt and Waylight palette rules belong to its original project.,~88:A CSS demo with blur or continuous motion may conflict with a strict-grid asset profile.];rq=[~72:Authoritative input or gameplay state and project-specific styling brief];so=[@s9607720391d7364f4ce0,@s2d1fa3b46950b17c2427,@sd346a4876cf1779a6b25,@s3401c0c3856b49d066ca];tg=[~21:state-driven-pixel-ui]}
@k.terrain-topology:K{ap=[roads_846bb37c,fences_d5624936,terrain_transitions_b20ad89c,autotiles_ca299e44];ck=[~79:Every declared pattern resolves or produces an explicit missing-pattern result.,~72:Adjacent edge or corner labels agree according to the selected topology.];nm=~50:Choose and exhaustively exercise tile connectivity;op=[~71:Define the bit ordering and which neighbor relations a tile represents.,~63:Enumerate the supported patterns and any intentional omissions.,~97:Verify selected tiles satisfy the neighborhood labels instead of guessing topology from an image.];pc=[@e.terrain-topology];rk=[~87:A 16-tile edge set, 16-tile corner set and 47-tile blob set encode different contracts.,~59:Do not assume every tile generator emits the same ordering.];rq=[~64:Named terrain labels and explicit edge, corner or mixed topology];so=[@s9607720391d7364f4ce0,@sfc536a697b0cf1c5c5aa,@sb4ca3e6ccb511b6af13d];tg=[~16:terrain-topology]}
@k.tile-repeat:K{ap=[seamless_textures_c8b9aaa4,floors_1d01b346,walls_5fbffcac,background_fills_b13f6457];ck=[~33:The declared edge relation holds.,~71:A native-scale neighborhood review checks visible seams and repetition.];nm=~40:Test repeating texture in a neighborhood;op=[~56:Design features that continue across wrapped boundaries.,~61:Render a 3x3 repetition and mark dominant repeated landmarks.,~124:For exact-match edge contracts compare opposite edge samples; for transition art inspect the declared continuation relation.];rk=[~83:Matching edge bytes is neither necessary nor sufficient for every seamless texture.,~61:Random interior noise does not automatically hide repetition.];rq=[~58:Tile dimensions and a declared edge-compatibility contract];so=[@s9607720391d7364f4ce0,@s4821777b3bd76181446e,@s332fbd8a75de6c3cf83e,@sa1afcd6f5fdb24235d9e];tg=[~11:tile-repeat]}
@k.tile-variants:K{ap=[repeated_terrain_1dfb8c05,biome_variants_6c1a9dfe,decorative_tile_reuse_cd70b901];ck=[~62:Variant selection never changes the required connection class.,~89:Same seed and inputs select the same sequence when deterministic generation is requested.];nm=~57:Vary interiors while preserving connectivity and lighting;op=[~46:Group variants by identical connection labels.,~77:Change interior details while keeping necessary boundary features compatible.,~88:Permit flips or rotations only when directional lighting and world meaning remain valid.];rk=[~56:Mirroring a shaded wall can reverse its light direction.,~92:Variant weights describe selection policy, not a guarantee of visual variety in a small map.];rq=[~68:A base topology, allowed transformations and seeded selection policy];so=[@s9607720391d7364f4ce0,@s4821777b3bd76181446e,@s358bfb37ab8702900eec,@s69253c5f8ee4510bdeb4];tg=[~13:tile-variants]}
